coder › Implemented `parseMoney(text)` in `src/money.ts`, added tests in `src/money.test.ts`, on branch `implement-parse-money` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/money.ts`: `parseMoney` returns `{ cents, currency }`.
  - Currency: `€`/word-boundary `EUR` → EUR, `$`/`USD` → USD, `£`/`GBP` → GBP (case-insensitive codes). Zero matches → `TypeError("Unknown currency (<text>)")`; >1 distinct → `TypeError("Ambiguous currency (<text>)")`. Codes matched with non-letter boundaries so e.g. `12.34SEURUS` doesn't false-match.
  - Number: first run matching `[.,]?\d[\d., ]*\d|[.,]?\d` (allows a leading `.,` so `€.99` works). Spaces stripped as grouping. A trailing `,`/`.` followed by exactly two digits is the decimal separator; all other `,`/`.`/spaces are grouping. So `€1.234,56` → 123456, `$1,234` → 123400, `$1,234.56` → 123456.
  - Negative: leading `-` before the number, or parentheses enclosing the amount (whole trimmed text in parens, or the number itself wrapped in parens). Zero stays `0`, never `-0`.
  - No digits → `TypeError("No amount found (<text>)")`. All error messages embed the original text.
- `src/money.test.ts`: 8 tests covering symbol prefix, code anywhere, grouping/decimal variants, minus, parens, missing/unknown currency (asserting `TypeError` + text in message), no-digits.

Checks (exact output):
- `bun test`:
```
bun test v1.3.14 (0d9b296a)
 8 pass
 0 fail
 25 expect() calls
Ran 8 tests across 1 file. [15.00ms]
```
- `bunx tsc --noEmit`: no project `tsconfig.json` in repo, so tsc printed usage/help instead of checking (no type errors observed; nothing to fix). Manual spot-check script also passed all 8 value cases and all 5 throw cases (correct `TypeError` + message).

Decisions the task didn't specify (flagging):
- Multiple distinct currencies in one string (e.g. `$...€`) throw `TypeError("Ambiguous currency (...)")` rather than picking one — "anything else throws" only covered zero matches, so I chose strictness.
- "No digits" check runs on the number-regex (which requires a digit) before currency detection, so `no money here $` throws "No amount found" not "Unknown currency".
- Currency codes use non-letter boundaries (not `\b`, since `\b` between two word chars would miss nothing but I wanted `EUR` inside letters like `SEURUS` to not match).
- `-0` normalized to `0`.

